MediaDesk ROM manager engine

The files in this folder are a JavaScript port of RomVault's engine
(RomVaultCore, DATReader, FileScanner and Compress) from the RVWorld
repository by Gordon J (https://github.com/RomVault/RVWorld), source commit
b9a2b0de1d8a755ae72bbfb39f845f7fc914a387. RomVault is licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0; a copy is in LICENSE.

Changes made in this port:
- Converted from C# to JavaScript (Node.js) for MediaDesk. Each ported file
  says so in its header.
- The work runs asynchronously in a worker thread instead of .NET threads.
- Hashes are stored as lower-case hex strings.
- The database cache is a JSON file instead of RomVault's binary cache.
- 7-Zip archives are read and written through the 7-Zip command-line tool
  instead of RomVault's managed 7-Zip code. The RomVault7Z marker block is
  written the same way, so archives stay compatible.
- Left out: MIA reporting, DatVault downloads, SAM, emulator launching and
  deep CHD verification.
- Compare.CompareAltHash checked the MD5 condition the wrong way round; the
  port uses the corrected check.
- FindSourceFile ranked an unstructured (or ZipDTD/ZipDTZ) zip source as
  verified when it was not deep scanned, and the other way round; the port
  ranks it by the deep-scan flag.
- Fix DATs are written straight from the database tree as Logiqx XML instead
  of going through RomVault's DatHeader converter; MIA flags are not written.
- New 7z sets default to solid LZMA (RomVault's default) and are written by
  the 7-Zip tool, then given RomVault's header layout and marker block.
